  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "tls: Workaround for missing handshake secret, app secret present",
  "description": "Mozilla NSS appears to have a bug when the ML-KEM key exchange support\nwas added so that the HANDSHAKE_TRAFFIC_SECRETs are not being written\nto the SSLKEYLOGFILE even though the other secrets like the application\nTRAFFIC_SECRET_0 are. Since the Finished message is always encrypted\nwith the handshake key, we'll never try to switch to the app traffic\nkey, even if we have it and could decrypt the TLS records that are\nencrypted using it.\n\nTo work around such situations, in TLS 1.3 if we fail to retrieve\nthe handshake traffic key, proceed to go ahead and try to retrieve\nthe appplication traffic key and store it for use against future TLS\nrecords. We won't decrypt records up to the Finished, but payload later\nwill be decrypted.\n\nWe don't need to do this for QUIC, which already retrieves the\nappropriate key based upon the type indicated in the packet header\n(Handshake vs Protected Payload.)\n\nWorkaround #20240",
